@node C33 Options
@section Options
@cindex C33 options
@cindex options for C33
@code{@value{AS}} supports the following additional command-line options
for the Seiko Epson S1C33 (C33) family of processors.  Without
@option{-mc33adv} or @option{-mc33pe} it assembles for the standard C33
core.

@cindex command-line options, C33
@cindex C33 command-line options
@table @code

@cindex @code{-mc33adv} command-line option, C33
@item -mc33adv
Assemble for the C33 Advanced core, accepting its additional
instructions and system registers.

@cindex @code{-mc33pe} command-line option, C33
@item -mc33pe
Assemble for the C33 PE core, accepting its additional instructions and
system registers.

The core is recorded in the top byte of the ELF header's @code{e_flags}:
0 for the standard core, @samp{A} for the Advanced core and @samp{P}
for the PE core.  The linker does not link objects built for different
cores.

@cindex @code{-medda32} command-line option, C33
@item -medda32
Do not use the default data area.  An @samp{x}-prefixed load, store or
bit instruction whose memory operand names a symbol, such as
@samp{xld.w %r4,[sym]}, then loads the symbol's absolute address into a
register and goes through that register: the destination register of a
load, or otherwise @code{%r0}, which is saved and restored around the
access with @code{pushn} and @code{popn}.  Without this option the
operand is reached at an offset from the default data pointer:
@code{%r15} with @code{doff_hi} and @code{doff_lo} on the standard and
PE cores, and @code{%dp} with @code{dpoff_h}, @code{dpoff_m} and
@code{dpoff_l} on the Advanced core.  @xref{C33 Opcodes}.

@cindex @code{-mfdpic} command-line option, C33
@item -mfdpic
Mark the object as FDPIC code, by setting @code{EF_C33_FDPIC} in the ELF
header's @code{e_flags}.  Only the @code{elf32-c33fdpic} target accepts
such objects, and the FDPIC linker does not accept objects without the
flag.  This is the default when @code{@value{AS}} is configured for
@samp{c33-*-linux-uclibc}.

@cindex @code{-mno-fdpic} command-line option, C33
@item -mno-fdpic
Do not mark the object as FDPIC code.
@end table

