@node C33-Chars
@subsection Special Characters

@cindex line comment character, C33
@cindex C33 line comment character
@samp{;} starts a comment anywhere on a line.

If a @samp{#} appears as the first character of a line, the whole line
is treated as a comment, but in this case the line can also be a
logical line number directive (@pxref{Comments}) or a preprocessor
control command (@pxref{Preprocessing}).

@cindex line separator, C33
@cindex statement separator, C33
@cindex C33 line separator
The @samp{`} character can be used to separate statements on the same
line, since @samp{;} starts a comment.

@node C33-Regs
@subsection Register Names

@cindex C33 register names
@cindex register names, C33
Register names start with @samp{%}.  The general registers are
@code{%r0} to @code{%r15}.  The system and special registers depend on
the core:

@table @asis
@item Every core
@code{%psr}, @code{%sp}, @code{%alr} and @code{%ahr}.

@item PE core
In addition, @code{%pc}, @code{%ttbr}, @code{%idir} and @code{%dbbr}.

@item Advanced core
In addition, @code{%pc}, @code{%ttbr}, @code{%idir}, @code{%dbbr},
@code{%lco}, @code{%lsa}, @code{%lea}, @code{%sor}, @code{%dp},
@code{%usp} and @code{%ssp}.
@end table

Which of them an instruction accepts depends on the instruction; for
example, on the PE core @code{pushs} and @code{pops} accept only
@code{%alr} and @code{%ahr}.

@node C33-Operands
@subsection Operands and Delay Slots

@cindex C33 operands
Operands are separated by commas, and the destination comes first:
@samp{ld.w %r4,%r5} copies @code{%r5} to @code{%r4}.  A memory operand
is written in brackets: @samp{[%r5]}, @samp{[%r5]+} (post-increment) or
@samp{[%sp+@var{offset}]}, where @var{offset} is in bytes.  The
@samp{x}-prefixed instructions also accept @samp{[%r@var{n}+@var{offset}]},
@samp{[@var{symbol}]} and @samp{[@var{symbol}+@var{offset}]}
(@pxref{C33 Opcodes}).

@cindex C33 delay slots
@cindex delay slots, C33
The suffix @samp{.d} on a branch, jump, call or return, as in
@samp{jrne.d}, @samp{call.d} or @samp{ret.d}, selects the delayed form:
the instruction that follows it runs before control is transferred.

@node C33 Floating Point
@section Floating Point

@cindex floating point, C33 (@sc{ieee})
@cindex C33 floating point (@sc{ieee})
The C33 family uses @sc{ieee} floating-point numbers, stored
